Description: Start commands run from the Shell in their systemd scope.
 A command run with Alt+F2, or by Util.spawn() and the other spawn helpers of js/misc/util.js, was spawned with
 Shell.util_spawn_async() and moved into a scope of its own, app-gnome-<program>-<pid>.scope, only once it ran, with
 gnome_start_systemd_scope(). systemd moves only the process it is given, so every process the command started in the
 meantime stayed in GNOME Shell's cgroup, and was stopped with GNOME Shell. The command is now launched like an
 application, through GDesktopAppInfo, which with the GLib of patches/glib2.0 puts it into its scope before it runs,
 and names the scope in the "launched" signal, for which leave-scope-to-glib.patch leaves it to GLib.
 .
 shell_util_spawn_command_async() builds the GAppInfo from the command line, quoting arguments where needed and
 escaping %, which starts a field code in the Exec key. The rlimit nofile is reset in the child as before, and the
 child stays a child of the Shell, which reaps it, as polkit relies on.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

